  {
   "id": "johansen test",
   "nombre_canonico": "Johansen test",
   "tipo": "metodo",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "Johansen test"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    77
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Test estadístico que evalúa el rango de cointegración operando directamente en series de precios I(1), ofreciendo múltiples vectores pero optimizando menos para el riesgo que OLS.",
     "doc_id": 77
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "The main advantage of the Johansen test over the Engle-Granger approach is the ability to perform hypothesis testings directly on I(1) price series themselves and derive cointegrating vectors without having to constantly check for stationarity.",
     "doc_id": 77
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "MIDE",
     "tipo_original": "MIDE",
     "objeto_texto": "cointegration",
     "doc_id": 77,
     "revisar": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "engle granger approach",
   "nombre_canonico": "Engle-Granger approach",
   "tipo": "metodo",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "Engle-Granger approach"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    77
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Método de regresión lineal para probar la cointegración, preferido por los autores porque minimiza la varianza del residual creando spreads más tratables para el riesgo.",
     "doc_id": 77
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "The classical approach for cointegration testing developed by Engle and Granger (1987) has the ability to capture long-term co-movements. We ﬁrst perform a linear regression on some given I(1) time series data, then test for stationarity of the residuals.",
     "doc_id": 77
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "USA",
     "tipo_original": "USA",
     "objeto_texto": "cointegration",
     "doc_id": 77,
     "revisar": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "markovian environment",
   "nombre_canonico": "Markovian environment",
   "tipo": "concepto",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "Markovian environment"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    78
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Factor estocástico exógeno que afecta el precio del activo financiero y captura la incertidumbre ambiental, descrito por un proceso generalizado de Ornstein-Uhlenbeck (OU).",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "The stochastic factor, which we refer to as the Markovian environment, is described by a generalized Ornstein–Uhlenbeck (OU) process.",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "PREDICE",
     "tipo_original": "PREDICE",
     "objeto_texto": "fundamental price",
     "doc_id": 78,
     "revisar": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "utility based statistical arbitrage",
   "nombre_canonico": "utility-based statistical arbitrage",
   "tipo": "concepto",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "utility-based statistical arbitrage"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    78
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Concepto de arbitraje estadístico basado en la maximización de utilidad esperada (CARA) en lugar de la minimización de costos esperados, implicando estrategias que incrementan la utilidad esperada mediante round-trip trading.",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "Intuitively, a financial market admits a utility-based statistical arbitrage for a large trader with CARA-type utility if there exists a trading strategy under which the sign of the initial inventory and that of a trading speed at some time differ, and by which the large trader can increase her expected utility.",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "USA",
     "tipo_original": "USA",
     "objeto_texto": "CARA utility",
     "doc_id": 78,
     "revisar": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "matrix riccati differential equation mrde",
   "nombre_canonico": "Matrix Riccati differential equation (MRDE)",
   "tipo": "metodo",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "Matrix Riccati differential equation (MRDE)"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    78
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Ecuación diferencial matricial que resulta del análisis de la ecuación HJB para encontrar la estrategia óptima. El paper prueba la existencia y unicidad de su solución bajo ciertas condiciones.",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "The time-dependent coefficients are determined by a solution to a system of numerically tractable ordinary differential equations (ODEs) ... consisting of (i) a matrix Riccati differential equation (MRDE)",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "PARTE_DE",
     "tipo_original": "PARTE_DE",
     "objeto_texto": "HJB equation",
     "doc_id": 78,
     "revisar": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "transient market impact",
   "nombre_canonico": "transient market impact",
   "tipo": "concepto",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "transient market impact"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    78
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Tipo de impacto de mercado que decae a lo largo de la ventana de trading. Representa un desbalance entre órdenes de compra y venta generado por la falta de liquidez por las ejecuciones de un large trader.",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "the transient market impact, recognized as a striking aspect of market impacts, is a type of market impact that decays over the trading window and is empirically confirmed",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "AFECTA",
     "tipo_original": "AFECTA",
     "objeto_texto": "market price",
     "doc_id": 78,
     "revisar": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hjb equation",
   "nombre_canonico": "HJB equation",
   "tipo": "metodo",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "HJB equation"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    78
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Ecuación de programación dinámica empleada para resolver el problema de control estocástico y encontrar la velocidad de ejecución óptima.",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "By analyzing the associated Hamilton–Jacobi–Bellman (HJB) equation, we derive an optimal execution strategy characterized by an affine function of the state variables",
     "doc_id": 78
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "USA",
     "tipo_original": "USA",
     "objeto_texto": "Matrix Riccati differential equation (MRDE)",
     "doc_id": 78,
     "revisar": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "market residual return",
   "nombre_canonico": "market residual return",
   "tipo": "concepto",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "market residual return"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    79
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Componente del retorno de una acción purgado del riesgo general del mercado al restarle el retorno del mercado ajustado por beta.",
     "doc_id": 79
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "First, we compute market residual returns, which are given by the difference between the stock returns and the product of the stock’s CAPM Fama and French (2004) equity beta and the market return.",
     "doc_id": 79
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "USA",
     "tipo_original": "USA",
     "objeto_texto": "correlation matrix",
     "doc_id": 79,
     "revisar": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "correlation matrix",
   "nombre_canonico": "correlation matrix",
   "tipo": "concepto",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "correlation matrix"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    79
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Matriz de similitud construida a partir de retornos residuales que contiene valores positivos y negativos, sirviendo como red signada para encontrar agrupaciones.",
     "doc_id": 79
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "Next, we compute the correlation matrix of residual returns, interpret it as a weighted signed network, and use graph clustering algorithms to partition the stocks into groups",
     "doc_id": 79
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
